# Nodes filaments: edge attach only

Hard rule for diana’s dashboard (`/Users/diana/my-dashboard`) **nodes** view filaments (`.aug20-edge` / `svg.aug20-zone-web`).

## Required behavior

- Filaments attach to each node’s **rim / perimeter** (nearest side toward the other node) via `rimPoint(nodeBox(...))`.
- They must **kiss the edge** of the node rectangle — not run through the photo into the geometric center.
- Style: soft continuous champagne filament (glow + orbs OK). **Never** white `stroke-dasharray` center-to-center stubs.

## Never

- `curve(a.pt, b.pt)` / `curve(A.pt, B.pt)` for filament paths (centers)
- Falling back to `A.pt` / `B.pt` when `nodeBox` fails — **skip** the edge instead
- `stroke-dasharray` on `.aug20-edge` (JS or CSS)
- Fixing only `everything.html` or only `prototype.html` — **both** must stay in sync (Diana often uses prototype; serve.py defaults to everything)

## Always

1. Keep `nodeBox` + `rimPoint` + draw loop that uses rim points only.
2. Keep `stroke-dasharray: none !important` on `path.aug20-edge`.
3. After any nodes / web / filament edit, hard-refresh **nodes** and confirm the filament meets the **sides** of two linked nodes (e.g. glow up → ambition), not their centers.
4. Click filament still removes; connect two nodes still works.

## If you see center attachment or dashed white lines through cards

Fix immediately in **both** `everything.html` and `prototype.html`. Do not wait to be reminded. This has regressed repeatedly from prototype/everything drift.
